;; Conformance fixture: machine/final-state-singleton-rests
;;
;; Per [005 §Final states](../../005-StateMachines.md#final-states-final--on-done--output-key).
;; A leaf state declares `:final? true`;
;; entering it completes the machine. A SINGLETON (non-spawned) machine
;; RESTS in its final state per D7: `:rf.machine/done` fires once, and the
;; snapshot stays readable; only a spawned actor is torn down at finality.
;;
;; This fixture exercises the pure-call surface: `machine-transition`
;; returns the post-transition `{:state :data}` snapshot. The pure
;; surface deliberately does NOT carry runtime-only metadata
;; (`:rf/finished?` etc.) — the lifecycle handler recomputes the
;; finality flag at the boundary. Hosts that exercise live semantics
;; observe the resting snapshot via the surrounding runtime; the pure
;; call here verifies the transition's state-shape.
;;
;; Per 005 §Final states D1: `:final?` is a first-class state-node key (NOT
;; stashed under `:meta`). Per D3: `:output-key` is a designated `:data`
;; slot, optional — when absent the parent's `:on-done` receives nil.

{:fixture/id           :machine/final-state-singleton-rests
 :fixture/spec-version "1.0"
 :fixture/capabilities #{:fsm/flat :fsm/final-states}
 :fixture/doc          "A singleton machine entering :final? produces a post-transition snapshot whose :state is the terminal leaf. Live hosts keep the singleton resting in it per D7; the pure surface here verifies the state-shape resolution. The :output-key slot is verified separately in final-state-child-fires-on-done."

 :fixture/registry
 {}

 :fixture/handlers
 {}

 :fixture/calls
 [;; (1) Transition into a :final? leaf. The post-transition snapshot's
  ;; :state IS the terminal leaf — verifies that the transition target
  ;; resolution respects `:final?` (which constrains the state-node's
  ;; shape — no :states / :initial / :on / :after / :always / :spawn).
  {:call         :machine-transition
   :definition
   {:initial :running
    :data    {:phase :idle}
    :states
    {:running {:on {:finish :done}}
     :done    {:final?     true
               :output-key :phase}}}
   :snapshot     {:state :running :data {:phase :working}}
   :event        [:finish]
   :expect-next-snapshot {:state :done :data {:phase :working}}
   :expect-effects       []}]}
